  "id": "BIT-seaweedfs-2026-129851",
  "summary": "SeaweedFS before 4.42 SSRF via VolumeServer.FetchAndWriteNeedle Replica URLs",
  "details": "SeaweedFS before 4.42 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in the VolumeServer.FetchAndWriteNeedle gRPC method that allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass the incomplete CVE-2026-73080 fix. Attackers can supply crafted replicas[].url entries or an azure_endpoint to make the volume server send requests with controlled tokens and bodies to internal services and metadata addresses.",
